& [PreservedQuestion] is exact
  + ProcedureType recursively contains ProcedureType through list and ordered-map member forms
  + ProcedureValue recursively contains ProcedureValue through list, ordered-map, record, and tagged-union forms
  + these types are reachable from public prepare, run, verify, and response contracts
  + the formed machine-schema profile rejects recursive definitions unless a finite resolved representation is separately proven
  + decide whether to use local recursive JSON Schema references, finite unrolling, or a separate finite transport projection

& [ObservedControls] are source facts to verify
  + cantor_core procedure validation caps maximum_call_depth at 64
  + type and value traversal decrement the supplied depth and fail at zero
  + bounded procedure values also enforce byte, collection-item, and map-entry ceilings
  + serde_json 1.0.151 uses a default JSON container recursion limit of 128 unless explicitly disabled
  + current public CLI decode does not disable that serde recursion limit

& [RequiredOutcome] is narrow
  + choose one deterministic recursive representation compatible with exact public serde forms
  + keep the schema document finite and content addressable
  + prevent network reference resolution and cycle-amplified generator traversal
  + separate JSON Schema acceptance, serde decode, and Cantor semantic depth enforcement
  + define conformance cases at, below, and beyond each applicable depth boundary
  - never: implement a schema generator, add a dependency, change a public form, weaken existing bounds, or activate CPMS-I02 from this source alone

